<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys May jet fuel below $204/tne in tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys May jet fuel below $204/tne in tender.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) bought by tender 32,000 tonnes of jet fuel at below $204 per tonne, for May 21-30 delivery, cost-and-freight (c-and-f) Keelung or Shen Ao, a CPC source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender, which closed on April 1, attracted 12 offers.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC bought two 32,000-tonne cargoes of jet fuel at $212.90 and $213.50 per tonne for end-April deliveries, c-and-f basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
